    {
      "id": "MPS-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-marked-period-finite-sheets",
      "title": "Finite representatives for the marked period lattices of a family",
      "hypotheses": "A smooth quasi-compact complex base of fixed relative dimension, a polarized abelian scheme of relative dimension g with order action of prescribed type, level N > 0, and sections killed by N. Every point has an admissible period and every admissible period is realized. Separation is required for the criterion for points. Full marking and N ≥ 3 are additionally required for the cited holomorphic dependence theorem.",
      "statement": "The distinct admissible marked isometry classes admitting a period are finite in number, bounded by the sum of the numbers of minimal primes of the rings of any finite affine cover. Separation gives a parametrization with the marked fibre criterion. At full level N ≥ 3 a fixed period and point determine the exponential uniquely.",
      "equations": [
        "lifts-marked-period-affine-bound"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "MPS-01"
      ],
